OL,3,AEurope is pouring billions into space.
OL,4,ACan Glasgow's satellite industry keep
OL,5,Aup?
OL,6,
OL,7,FEurope is pouring billions into space.
OL,8,FCan Glasgow's satellite industry keep
OL,9,Fup?
OL,11,FIn 2005, a young space engineer called
OL,12,FCraig Clark moved back to his home city
OL,13,Fof Glasgow. He'd graduated from
OL,14,Funiversity just over a decade before,
OL,15,Fbut the only jobs he could find were
OL,16,Fsouth of the border. Now Craig wanted
OL,17,Fto start a company of his own. He
OL,18,Fcalled it Clyde Space.
OL,23,APub: 05-OctQpppppppppppppppppppppG13/39
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,315,300,200,140,0,100
PN,11914
SC,0014
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F119A1791263967
OL,1,W5j 5Q7kjs15j 5ws
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q%**,$-.,%,. (,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,AEurope is pouring billions into space.
OL,4,ACan Glasgow's satellite industry keep
OL,5,Aup?
OL,6,
OL,7,FI went to school not far from the River
OL,8,FClyde, where the city's shipbuilding
OL,9,Fheritage was forged, and knew Glasgow
OL,10,Fhad once been an industrial powerhouse.
OL,11,FWhen I was a child, "Clyde-built"
OL,12,Freally meant something: craftsmanship
OL,13,Fand engineering excellence. There was a
OL,14,Fsaying that I grew up with: "The Clyde
OL,15,Fmade Glasgow and Glasgow made the
OL,16,FClyde."
OL,18,FWhat I hadn't realised until recently
OL,19,Fwas that, in a different guise, that
OL,20,Ftradition is still alive. Two decades
OL,21,Flater, Glasgow is a European leader in
OL,22,Fbuilding small satellites.
OL,23,APub: 05-OctQpppppppppppppppppppppG14/39
